1
00:00:05,730 --> 00:00:07,670
So what did you and Star talk about?

2
00:00:08,200 --> 00:00:09,630
I think I'm heartbroken.

3
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:13,470
I don't get why you'd stress this much over Star.

4
00:00:13,470 --> 00:00:17,630
Because to me, you as you are right now is already the best there is.

5
00:00:18,630 --> 00:00:20,000
You like Fuen, don't you?

6
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:20,930
Do I have to answer?

7
00:00:21,200 --> 00:00:24,870
You don't have to answer. But you should know — I like Fuen.

8
00:00:24,870 --> 00:00:27,530
Do what you want. You won't win Fuen over anyway.

9
00:00:27,530 --> 00:00:28,970
I'm going after him either way.

10
00:00:29,500 --> 00:00:30,900
Then why'd you join the club?

11
00:00:30,900 --> 00:00:32,870
I get lonely. I wanted to be with friends.

12
00:00:33,230 --> 00:00:36,330
We've got M.4 juniors signing up as staff. Let's give them a hand.

13
00:00:42,070 --> 00:00:43,030
Chemi.

14
00:00:43,430 --> 00:00:45,900
After practice today, don't rush off.

15
00:00:46,070 --> 00:00:49,600
And what if I want a boyfriend too? Do I have to wait until secondary school?

16
00:00:49,600 --> 00:00:52,970
If you don't have anyone by then, I'll be your first boyfriend myself.

17
00:00:52,970 --> 00:00:57,530
Aof, back then you told me once I got to upper secondary...

18
00:01:01,430 --> 00:01:03,600
Star, I'm really sorry we didn't tell you first.

19
00:01:03,600 --> 00:01:06,100
But if it isn't you, honestly, it can't be anyone else.

20
00:01:06,100 --> 00:01:09,100
I'll be straight with you — I'm not confident I can pull it off.

21
00:01:09,100 --> 00:01:11,030
Either way, we'd never abandon you.

22
00:01:11,030 --> 00:01:12,270
I'll do it.

23
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:17,100
Yes! Thank you so much.

24
00:01:31,900 --> 00:01:32,970
You like Fuen, don't you?

25
00:01:33,370 --> 00:01:34,370
So what?

26
00:01:38,630 --> 00:01:39,970
Do I have to tell you?

27
00:01:40,270 --> 00:01:41,270
You don't have to.

28
00:01:43,800 --> 00:01:46,970
But you should know — I like Fuen.

29
00:01:47,530 --> 00:01:49,170
I'm going after Fuen either way.

30
00:01:49,170 --> 00:01:50,870
Do what you want. / Let's play it fair.

31
00:01:50,870 --> 00:01:52,700
You won't win him over. So you're serious.

32
00:01:52,700 --> 00:01:55,030
Fair and square. I'm going after him either way.

33
00:01:55,030 --> 00:01:56,729
Because I like Fuen.

34
00:01:56,729 --> 00:01:57,770
Argh!

35
00:02:02,070 --> 00:02:04,530
What's wrong with you? Bad dream?

36
00:02:06,870 --> 00:02:09,229
It's a day off. I want to sleep.

37
00:02:12,030 --> 00:02:17,370
Yeah, a nightmare. And you were in it. / Uh-huh.

38
00:02:17,370 --> 00:02:22,000
I dreamed I saw you running through Siam in a monkey suit.

39
00:02:23,100 --> 00:02:25,700
And I was chasing you. But here's the thing—

40
00:02:25,700 --> 00:02:28,370
somehow you had a whole crowd into you.

41
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:31,530
And they were all running after you and me.

42
00:02:32,230 --> 00:02:33,670
Gave me a splitting headache.

43
00:02:34,500 --> 00:02:36,300
Doesn't that count as a nightmare?

44
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:42,970
Oh, Physics, buddy.

45
00:02:44,270 --> 00:02:47,270
There, there. You poor thing.

46
00:02:48,030 --> 00:02:49,000
Terrifying, huh?

47
00:02:51,130 --> 00:02:52,370
Ugh, what a nightmare.

48
00:02:52,370 --> 00:02:54,300
Quit messing with me.

49
00:02:59,900 --> 00:03:01,770
Who's making all that noise this early?

50
00:03:01,770 --> 00:03:03,570
It's a day off!

51
00:03:13,930 --> 00:03:15,400
Whoa! Din!

52
00:03:52,500 --> 00:03:53,930
What's up with you?

53
00:03:55,900 --> 00:03:57,000
Nothing.

54
00:03:57,600 --> 00:03:59,370
That monkey thing's still bugging me.

55
00:04:05,100 --> 00:04:06,930
Come on. Shower.

56
00:06:10,500 --> 00:06:13,070
Din, how do you like living here, sweetie?

57
00:06:13,070 --> 00:06:16,770
It's your mom, dear. She never asks anyone before she does anything.

58
00:06:16,770 --> 00:06:19,130
Hold on — you're the one who talked me into buying it.

59
00:06:19,130 --> 00:06:20,400
Did I?

60
00:06:22,500 --> 00:06:27,900
It's great, Aunt Pat. Living this close to Fuen, I won't get lonely.

61
00:06:27,900 --> 00:06:29,530
And we can talk things over whenever.

62
00:06:29,530 --> 00:06:33,730
Fuen, giving advice? He can barely keep himself afloat.

63
00:06:33,730 --> 00:06:37,270
Mom! I'm your son. How can you say that?

64
00:06:37,270 --> 00:06:40,230
You gave birth to me yourself. Same blood and everything.

65
00:06:40,830 --> 00:06:43,370
Aunt Om, listen to how my mom talks to me.

66
00:06:43,870 --> 00:06:45,530
How can you say that about your son?

67
00:06:45,530 --> 00:06:48,330
Well, am I wrong? Right, Din?

68
00:06:50,270 --> 00:06:51,300
Sure, I guess.

69
00:06:56,700 --> 00:06:59,030
Physics, aren't you eating? Come here.

70
00:06:59,570 --> 00:07:04,770
Uh... I'd better not. My stomach's a bit off.

71
00:07:05,130 --> 00:07:07,070
I'll just step out to the restroom.

72
00:07:12,800 --> 00:07:13,800
Thank you.

73
00:07:16,530 --> 00:07:18,230
Here, Fuen. Take this.

74
00:07:19,400 --> 00:07:21,000
Whoa. / Eat up.

75
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:22,830
Have some fish, dear. Some fish.

76
00:07:23,770 --> 00:07:25,500
This one too. Here, here.

77
00:07:25,500 --> 00:07:26,970
Avocado, sweetie.

78
00:07:27,700 --> 00:07:29,500
Careful, you'll stain your shirt.

79
00:07:29,500 --> 00:07:30,900
Here, shrimp.

80
00:07:42,300 --> 00:07:43,970
Mom. / What is it, dear?

81
00:07:43,970 --> 00:07:48,370
I'm going to wash my hands. Be right back.

82
00:07:59,500 --> 00:08:04,030
Good, dear. Eat plenty. This place is so good.

83
00:08:32,700 --> 00:08:35,130
I knew your stomach was fine.

84
00:08:36,929 --> 00:08:41,669
What's with you today? You've been quiet since dinner.

85
00:08:44,530 --> 00:08:52,570
It's nothing. Your two families are just so close.

86
00:08:52,570 --> 00:08:56,100
I'm the outsider. I couldn't follow. Had nothing to add.

87
00:08:57,370 --> 00:09:06,630
Or, like, ask me what I want to be when I grow up, my dream job, that kind of thing.

88
00:09:06,630 --> 00:09:08,100
Are you messing with me?

89
00:09:12,500 --> 00:09:15,630
Out! / Nope!

90
00:09:19,330 --> 00:09:20,570
Fine, it's out.

91
00:09:20,570 --> 00:09:21,930
It's out now. / Yeah.

92
00:09:21,930 --> 00:09:23,570
Right? / Did you even wash your hands?

93
00:09:23,570 --> 00:09:24,770
I did.

94
00:09:28,070 --> 00:09:29,870
What's going on with you today?

95
00:09:29,870 --> 00:09:33,730
Normally when I talk with Tang and Aof about stuff that has nothing to do with you,

96
00:09:33,730 --> 00:09:35,770
you're all over it with questions.

97
00:09:36,330 --> 00:09:38,530
You're being weird today.

98
00:09:47,630 --> 00:09:49,230
If something's wrong, tell me.

99
00:09:51,030 --> 00:09:52,700
Nothing's wrong.

100
00:09:53,070 --> 00:09:54,130
You sure?

101
00:09:55,900 --> 00:09:57,170
Positive?

102
00:09:59,730 --> 00:10:01,600
Come to Siam with me.

103
00:10:03,570 --> 00:10:07,230
I just want to be around you. Humor me, okay?

104
00:10:11,470 --> 00:10:12,930
After we eat, then.

105
00:10:14,200 --> 00:10:18,800
Fine, I'll humor you. But let me be a good son first.

106
00:10:20,070 --> 00:10:21,030
Deal.

107
00:10:22,270 --> 00:10:24,170
Back to dinner.

108
00:10:26,270 --> 00:10:28,000
Can I order another steak?

109
00:10:29,700 --> 00:10:31,400
Ask my mom.

110
00:11:00,130 --> 00:11:01,770
"Hey, Chat,"

111
00:11:01,770 --> 00:11:05,070
"as someone who's cute, kind-hearted, and studies hard,"

112
00:11:05,070 --> 00:11:09,070
"I want to know — on my first day in the football club, will I get lucky in love?"

113
00:11:11,800 --> 00:11:13,500
Hey, Chemi, what are you doing?

114
00:11:13,900 --> 00:11:16,600
"What an excellent question..."

115
00:11:16,930 --> 00:11:18,130
So slow.

116
00:11:19,530 --> 00:11:21,200
Hey, when did you even get here?

117
00:11:21,630 --> 00:11:22,930
What about Est and Jay?

118
00:11:22,930 --> 00:11:24,230
They went on ahead.

119
00:11:31,170 --> 00:11:32,970
Who are you texting? So serious.

120
00:11:39,570 --> 00:11:45,170
Chat gives real advice. Helps with everything. And best of all—

121
00:11:45,170 --> 00:11:46,500
never nags me once.

122
00:11:48,330 --> 00:11:50,700
I don't nag you either, do I?

123
00:11:55,000 --> 00:11:57,430
What's going on? Why not talk to me about it?

124
00:12:02,100 --> 00:12:02,900
Well...

125
00:12:06,230 --> 00:12:09,130
Remember what I told you about, back when I was a kid—

126
00:12:09,130 --> 00:12:10,870
some guy promised he'd go after me?

127
00:12:11,730 --> 00:12:12,900
Oh, you mean Aof.

128
00:12:12,900 --> 00:12:13,430
Huh?!

129
00:12:14,700 --> 00:12:17,030
Shit... How did you know?

130
00:12:17,030 --> 00:12:18,270
I'm your friend, aren't I?

131
00:12:19,230 --> 00:12:23,570
At first we couldn't decide whether it was Tang or Aof.

132
00:12:25,770 --> 00:12:28,800
But seeing you join a club you're terrible at,

133
00:12:29,300 --> 00:12:31,030
I figured it out. Only one reason.

134
00:12:36,070 --> 00:12:42,730
Yeah, that's it. What stresses me out is I'm in upper secondary now,

135
00:12:43,770 --> 00:12:48,170
and I don't have anyone, but Aof still hasn't made a move.

136
00:12:50,500 --> 00:12:52,430
That's why I'm asking Chat.

137
00:12:53,670 --> 00:12:55,470
In case I should make the first move.

138
00:12:58,700 --> 00:13:02,070
Are you even sure he isn't talking to someone already?

139
00:13:03,070 --> 00:13:05,670
Maybe the reason he hasn't made a move

140
00:13:08,730 --> 00:13:10,030
is that he's not single.

141
00:13:17,670 --> 00:13:20,470
Give it here! I'll check for you.

142
00:13:22,500 --> 00:13:24,700
If he's already seeing someone,

143
00:13:24,700 --> 00:13:26,930
his friends would be gossiping about it, right?

144
00:13:29,730 --> 00:13:36,500
And if there's nothing at all, that means he was never serious about you.

145
00:13:38,400 --> 00:13:41,930
You're... even more brutal than Chat.

146
00:13:46,770 --> 00:13:48,570
Go on, go on.

147
00:13:58,270 --> 00:13:59,100
Aof!

148
00:14:02,270 --> 00:14:04,100
Hey, Mii!

149
00:14:04,100 --> 00:14:05,330
You came after all?

150
00:14:05,330 --> 00:14:09,270
Of course. I wasn't going to, but Rei asked me, so here I am.

151
00:14:09,700 --> 00:14:11,570
But when I asked, you wouldn't come.

152
00:14:11,570 --> 00:14:12,670
Only a little.

153
00:14:13,230 --> 00:14:14,870
You're so whipped.

154
00:14:14,870 --> 00:14:16,400
Enough. Let's take a picture.

155
00:14:28,900 --> 00:14:30,500
I'll tag you. / Sure.

156
00:14:36,870 --> 00:14:38,070
Yeah, got it.

157
00:14:40,200 --> 00:14:42,570
I'm off. Play hard out there, kid.

158
00:14:42,970 --> 00:14:43,970
Let's catch up later.

159
00:14:43,970 --> 00:14:45,170
Yeah, see you.

160
00:14:49,030 --> 00:14:51,330
Shit.

161
00:14:57,870 --> 00:15:00,570
Zac, you went too far, man.

162
00:15:02,070 --> 00:15:05,870
So were you guessing back there, or do you know something you're not telling me?

163
00:15:06,730 --> 00:15:09,900
Whoa, easy. I don't know anything about Aof.

164
00:15:10,530 --> 00:15:13,900
They could just be friends. Why don't you ask Physics?

165
00:15:13,900 --> 00:15:18,600
No way. If my brother finds out, he'll kill me.

166
00:15:26,230 --> 00:15:31,570
Help me out. With this hanging over me, I can't function.

167
00:15:32,800 --> 00:15:36,930
Uh-huh. Enough, buddy. Go talk to your Chat. I'm out.

168
00:15:37,970 --> 00:15:38,800
Chat.

169
00:15:40,270 --> 00:15:41,670
Hey, hurry up and follow me.

170
00:15:43,500 --> 00:15:44,900
We're late for the field.

171
00:15:53,070 --> 00:15:57,230
"My advice is to focus on your studies first."

172
00:16:07,770 --> 00:16:09,900
Thank you. Thank you.

173
00:16:09,900 --> 00:16:15,730
But I think the activity you've planned costs too much.

174
00:16:17,730 --> 00:16:21,570
And the point of this camp is for seniors and juniors to get to know each other better.

175
00:16:21,570 --> 00:16:26,630
Which means we don't need somewhere far away. Somewhere closer would save the budget.

176
00:16:26,630 --> 00:16:28,670
I think you should go rethink it.

177
00:16:34,370 --> 00:16:36,730
But I've thought all of this through very carefully.

178
00:16:37,370 --> 00:16:39,770
And I think the price is reasonable.

179
00:16:41,830 --> 00:16:45,100
But if you think any part is too much, Din, I can cover it myself.

180
00:16:45,700 --> 00:16:48,370
You think everyone would be glad to take your money?

181
00:16:53,700 --> 00:16:56,230
Then tell me what you want me to do.

182
00:17:04,030 --> 00:17:09,700
That's your problem. If you won't change it, you have to find the money to cover it.

183
00:17:10,829 --> 00:17:13,270
And obviously, not your family's money.

184
00:17:15,569 --> 00:17:19,000
Once you find a way, I'll reconsider.

185
00:17:20,300 --> 00:17:23,430
You said it. Because I will find a way.

186
00:17:26,170 --> 00:17:27,630
Then I'll take my leave.

187
00:17:30,170 --> 00:17:31,870
Let's go, Time.

188
00:17:33,530 --> 00:17:35,470
I'll smooth it over. Chill.

189
00:17:35,800 --> 00:17:36,630
Star.

190
00:17:40,430 --> 00:17:41,570
Star.

191
00:17:42,800 --> 00:17:47,030
Time, I shouldn't have argued with him like that.

192
00:17:50,270 --> 00:17:53,000
I already figured you didn't have a plan.

193
00:17:53,630 --> 00:17:55,300
And you still acted tough with him.

194
00:17:55,700 --> 00:17:57,170
It's just, like...

195
00:17:57,770 --> 00:17:59,470
Don't even. Come on.

196
00:17:59,470 --> 00:18:00,570
You're buying dessert.

197
00:18:01,100 --> 00:18:02,930
Ugh, seriously.

198
00:18:04,500 --> 00:18:06,070
Oh, Din.

199
00:18:07,130 --> 00:18:09,700
That kid Star is exactly like you, Din.

200
00:18:11,630 --> 00:18:13,430
Same way you argued with the seniors.

201
00:18:13,870 --> 00:18:15,100
But I had my reasons.

202
00:18:15,500 --> 00:18:17,030
Your own reasons, sure.

203
00:18:17,030 --> 00:18:20,800
And after you were done arguing, you'd sit outside moping like a kicked puppy.

204
00:18:22,630 --> 00:18:26,730
I've still got the photo, you know. Hold on, let me find it.

205
00:18:28,670 --> 00:18:31,500
Here. Look at your face, Din.

206
00:18:32,430 --> 00:18:34,770
You turned around looking mad at me, too.

207
00:18:34,770 --> 00:18:36,830
Arguing exactly the way Star does.

208
00:18:38,770 --> 00:18:42,100
I told you I can do it. Why won't you let me?

209
00:18:42,100 --> 00:18:44,630
Because what you're planning is too big.

210
00:18:45,370 --> 00:18:48,170
I don't see why we need to take everyone out of province.

211
00:18:48,170 --> 00:18:50,970
Not to mention the costs. It's a waste.

212
00:18:50,970 --> 00:18:53,700
And I told you, I'll find the money to cover it myself.

213
00:18:53,700 --> 00:18:55,370
Are you even listening to me?

214
00:18:55,370 --> 00:18:57,330
Din! You are unbelievable—

215
00:19:01,870 --> 00:19:03,570
Fine... let's hear it.

216
00:19:05,070 --> 00:19:08,630
I have my own way. You don't need to know.

217
00:19:13,200 --> 00:19:14,500
Hilarious, isn't it?

218
00:19:16,200 --> 00:19:17,500
We planned it together.

219
00:19:17,930 --> 00:19:19,270
You all wanted to go.

220
00:19:20,170 --> 00:19:21,900
And you left me to fight it out alone.

221
00:19:21,900 --> 00:19:24,700
Hey, you're our only hope.

222
00:19:26,600 --> 00:19:30,700
Just now, you could tell he only said that to beat you.

223
00:19:30,700 --> 00:19:33,600
He doesn't actually want to go ask his dad for money.

224
00:19:34,100 --> 00:19:38,770
Let's hope you're right. And next year we need someone to take over my job.

225
00:19:39,570 --> 00:19:41,270
Who do you think we should push?

226
00:19:41,270 --> 00:19:42,300
Star.

227
00:19:44,300 --> 00:19:46,370
He's not on the student council.

228
00:19:46,370 --> 00:19:47,430
So what?

229
00:19:48,600 --> 00:19:52,400
There's no rule saying you have to have been on the council from the start.

230
00:19:54,570 --> 00:19:57,230
People just want someone like you, don't they?

231
00:19:58,900 --> 00:20:01,530
Someone they can trust and feel at ease with.

232
00:20:02,900 --> 00:20:05,900
So do you think Star can be like me?

233
00:20:05,900 --> 00:20:06,800
He can.

234
00:20:10,830 --> 00:20:13,100
I don't mind you all rooting for him.

235
00:20:14,530 --> 00:20:17,730
But he has to show me he can really do it.

236
00:20:20,070 --> 00:20:22,300
So I know I'm not picking the wrong person.

237
00:20:22,600 --> 00:20:25,170
Ugh. What a show-off.

238
00:20:39,200 --> 00:20:42,270
So what do you want me to humor you with today?

239
00:20:43,470 --> 00:20:45,030
Today?

240
00:20:51,130 --> 00:20:55,230
A movie. The one you said you wanted to see.

241
00:20:55,930 --> 00:20:57,900
It opens today. First day.

242
00:20:57,900 --> 00:20:59,370
Are you serious?

243
00:20:59,770 --> 00:21:01,630
Wait, you actually remembered?

244
00:21:02,600 --> 00:21:05,230
I said that ages ago, didn't I?

245
00:21:07,400 --> 00:21:10,730
Just so you know how much attention I pay to you.

246
00:21:15,630 --> 00:21:19,270
Right... Come on, my treat.

247
00:21:21,300 --> 00:21:25,130
Too late for that, kid.

248
00:21:25,130 --> 00:21:27,470
I already bought the tickets online.

249
00:21:28,900 --> 00:21:33,500
And the important part — popcorn, half cheese, half sweet.

250
00:21:33,500 --> 00:21:35,100
Exactly the way you like it.

251
00:21:35,100 --> 00:21:36,400
Whoa.

252
00:21:40,170 --> 00:21:42,900
You really are the friend who knows me best.

253
00:21:42,900 --> 00:21:44,930
It's nothing. / Let's go watch.

254
00:21:44,930 --> 00:21:45,870
Wait.

255
00:21:47,100 --> 00:21:50,570
If we're seeing a movie together, we're at least taking a picture.

256
00:21:50,570 --> 00:21:51,670
Come on.

257
00:22:06,770 --> 00:22:09,530
Let me put it on my story first.

258
00:22:09,530 --> 00:22:12,030
Ugh, you can post while we walk.

259
00:22:17,870 --> 00:22:20,700
Sir, these are the seats I booked.

260
00:23:16,700 --> 00:23:20,230
Thanks for bringing me.

261
00:23:51,530 --> 00:23:56,730
Here, eat something first. Get some sugar in you.

262
00:23:56,730 --> 00:23:59,100
I already got Booboo and Teu on board.

263
00:24:01,230 --> 00:24:03,730
You think everyone would be glad to take your money?

264
00:24:03,730 --> 00:24:06,370
Then tell me what you want me to do.

265
00:24:06,370 --> 00:24:08,870
Time, do you think Din is picking on me on purpose?

266
00:24:09,270 --> 00:24:10,330
Star.

267
00:24:10,330 --> 00:24:12,630
Here I thought you were worried about the money.

268
00:24:13,330 --> 00:24:17,700
I am. But like, when you pitch an idea in that room,

269
00:24:17,700 --> 00:24:19,670
does Din always shoot you down?

270
00:24:19,670 --> 00:24:23,470
Or does he think being student council president means he can do whatever he wants?

271
00:24:24,400 --> 00:24:26,670
You're mad enough to start calling him names?

272
00:24:27,630 --> 00:24:29,270
In my head it's way worse than that.

273
00:24:30,670 --> 00:24:33,800
Whatever, forget it. I don't want to talk about it anymore.

274
00:24:35,100 --> 00:24:37,630
Let's think about how to actually pull this off.

275
00:24:38,330 --> 00:24:42,670
I want to prove myself. That I can do it no matter what.

276
00:25:00,430 --> 00:25:02,070
Is it good?

277
00:25:07,530 --> 00:25:12,470
Even though today isn't a real match, I want all of you to give it everything.

278
00:25:13,470 --> 00:25:15,200
Understood?

279
00:25:15,200 --> 00:25:17,030
Yes, Coach.

280
00:25:41,900 --> 00:25:45,200
What's with that face? You were fine this morning.

281
00:25:46,030 --> 00:25:48,670
Those guys were messing with me a bit.

282
00:25:51,500 --> 00:25:54,630
So what are you planning, Rei? Today's just a warm-up.

283
00:25:54,970 --> 00:25:56,930
Do you know what I'm planning, Mii?

284
00:25:58,000 --> 00:26:00,600
You don't. Which means I'm not planning anything.

285
00:26:01,200 --> 00:26:02,630
Rei.

286
00:26:08,300 --> 00:26:10,300
You should go sit over there, though.

287
00:26:10,300 --> 00:26:11,570
The sun's harsh out here.

288
00:26:11,570 --> 00:26:13,300
Not really the place for you.

289
00:26:14,730 --> 00:26:15,930
Come on.

290
00:26:17,630 --> 00:26:21,200
Listen up. Give it everything. Tear them apart.

291
00:26:21,200 --> 00:26:22,130
Got it?

292
00:26:23,030 --> 00:26:26,300
One, two, three... Thapfah! Hey!

293
00:26:26,300 --> 00:26:27,970
Suan Mali! Hey!

294
00:26:31,170 --> 00:26:35,930
Aof and Thanop are so cool. Just standing there, you can tell they're the top guys.

295
00:26:35,930 --> 00:26:36,900
True.

296
00:26:38,230 --> 00:26:40,730
I say our team's got this in the bag.

297
00:26:41,630 --> 00:26:42,900
I wouldn't be so sure.

298
00:26:43,630 --> 00:26:45,370
See their captain over there?

299
00:26:45,600 --> 00:26:46,970
The other side's stacked too.

300
00:26:46,970 --> 00:26:48,730
That guy's name is Rei.

301
00:26:48,730 --> 00:26:52,200
If he gets serious, Aof and Thanop are in for a rough time.

302
00:26:52,200 --> 00:26:53,300
How so, sir?

303
00:26:54,370 --> 00:26:56,630
He can hold his own. Hard to read.

304
00:26:57,570 --> 00:26:59,930
He plays on emotion.

305
00:26:59,930 --> 00:27:01,600
Not dirty, though.

306
00:27:01,600 --> 00:27:04,170
But he's good.

307
00:27:21,270 --> 00:27:23,600
Move up! Move up!

308
00:27:52,570 --> 00:27:55,200
Hey, close him down!

309
00:28:09,200 --> 00:28:10,430
Damn it.

310
00:28:13,530 --> 00:28:15,300
That guy's the real deal. / Yeah, he is.

311
00:28:15,300 --> 00:28:16,730
He's so good.

312
00:28:41,000 --> 00:28:42,300
Aof, pass it!

313
00:29:04,500 --> 00:29:08,330
What do we do, Star, if we can't come up with the money?

314
00:29:09,570 --> 00:29:12,270
Should we work out a new plan to pitch instead?

315
00:29:14,100 --> 00:29:17,800
No. There has to be a way.

316
00:29:17,800 --> 00:29:21,570
Otherwise, where did the seniors get the money to take us last year?

317
00:29:23,600 --> 00:29:26,500
I never knew money was this hard to come by.

318
00:29:27,000 --> 00:29:29,030
Huge respect to anyone good at making it.

319
00:29:30,000 --> 00:29:32,370
It's making me miss my mom and dad.

320
00:29:33,100 --> 00:29:36,000
Right? I should thank my parents for raising me so well.

321
00:29:36,000 --> 00:29:37,800
And I still give them hell daily.

322
00:29:39,170 --> 00:29:42,070
Let's grab something nice to drink first. Cool our heads.

323
00:29:43,600 --> 00:29:45,930
Oh. / Hey.

324
00:29:45,930 --> 00:29:47,800
Star, what are you doing here?

325
00:29:47,800 --> 00:29:50,770
We just finished dessert. We're heading back.

326
00:29:50,770 --> 00:29:53,230
And what's FUN VIBE doing here?

327
00:29:53,230 --> 00:29:57,370
We came to shoot content. Just waiting for the sun to drop a bit.

328
00:29:58,800 --> 00:30:00,900
Then can we come watch?

329
00:30:00,900 --> 00:30:02,230
Sure.

330
00:30:02,530 --> 00:30:03,870
Where at?

331
00:30:04,300 --> 00:30:09,130
We haven't figured that out. We know we're shooting, we just don't know where.

332
00:30:12,570 --> 00:30:13,930
Oh, come on.

333
00:30:14,600 --> 00:30:17,170
Then I know a good spot.

334
00:30:20,030 --> 00:30:22,030
You really haven't seen it?

335
00:30:23,630 --> 00:30:26,000
Get ready — you'll get your content.

336
00:31:18,630 --> 00:31:20,300
Ball!

337
00:31:45,470 --> 00:31:47,600
Where the hell were you aiming?

338
00:32:05,870 --> 00:32:09,270
I'm surprised you don't know football is a team sport.

339
00:32:09,270 --> 00:32:10,670
Rei, you asshole!

340
00:32:11,300 --> 00:32:12,270
Who?

341
00:32:12,270 --> 00:32:14,770
Aof! Aof! / What?

342
00:32:15,300 --> 00:32:16,700
Aof, stop!

343
00:32:16,700 --> 00:32:17,600
Stop.

344
00:32:19,800 --> 00:32:22,730
Suan Mali, you can head back. The match is over.

345
00:32:23,500 --> 00:32:24,570
Let's go.

346
00:32:37,870 --> 00:32:41,430
Why are you stopping me, Coach? You saw him kick me. Did you see it?

347
00:32:42,130 --> 00:32:46,300
You're angry at what he said because it's true, Aof.

348
00:32:46,300 --> 00:32:47,970
But Coach, he played dirty.

349
00:32:49,000 --> 00:32:51,800
If you could see how you played today,

350
00:32:51,800 --> 00:32:55,070
you wouldn't be sitting here arguing nonsense, Aof.

351
00:32:56,870 --> 00:32:59,400
But if you think you played well,

352
00:32:59,400 --> 00:33:01,400
turn around and look at your teammates.

353
00:33:01,400 --> 00:33:02,770
See the state of them?

354
00:33:06,800 --> 00:33:10,000
Then tell me what you actually got out of today.

355
00:33:11,870 --> 00:33:13,330
Go rest, Aof.

356
00:33:14,100 --> 00:33:17,470
I think you've learned your lesson. The team lost...

357
00:33:24,500 --> 00:33:27,900
You lot too. Go rest, you've had enough. / Yes, sir.

358
00:34:06,530 --> 00:34:11,230
Have some cold water. It'll cool you down.

359
00:34:25,000 --> 00:34:26,070
Thanks.

360
00:34:27,830 --> 00:34:30,630
You did your best today, Aof.

361
00:34:32,570 --> 00:34:35,199
No, I didn't. I lost the team the match.

362
00:34:35,199 --> 00:34:36,969
I let my emotions run the game.

363
00:34:38,530 --> 00:34:39,800
Aof.

364
00:34:41,270 --> 00:34:45,830
If it were me and I ran into a guy like that, and he shoulder-checked me—

365
00:34:45,830 --> 00:34:50,730
I'd kick his leg out, then punch him in the face until it hurt.

366
00:34:52,130 --> 00:34:56,170
Then I'd grab a stick and just start swinging,

367
00:34:56,170 --> 00:34:59,170
until he couldn't play anymore. And if he still didn't stop,

368
00:34:59,170 --> 00:35:02,770
I'd pepper-spray him right in the face so he couldn't see a thing.

369
00:35:02,770 --> 00:35:05,930
Guys like that deserve exactly that.

370
00:35:12,170 --> 00:35:14,070
So how are you getting home today, Chemi?

371
00:35:14,070 --> 00:35:16,030
I'll head back with my friends.

372
00:35:17,130 --> 00:35:18,400
Let me take you.

373
00:35:20,270 --> 00:35:22,670
It's all right, I'll go with my friends.

374
00:35:32,430 --> 00:35:34,370
Let me take you home, Chemi.

375
00:35:34,770 --> 00:35:37,930
I really want to be with you today.

376
00:35:37,930 --> 00:35:39,830
Consider it cheering me up.

377
00:35:47,400 --> 00:35:48,730
Please...

378
00:35:50,100 --> 00:35:51,700
Okay.

379
00:35:51,700 --> 00:35:54,100
Consider it cheering you up.

380
00:36:30,100 --> 00:36:31,370
You think it's nice?

381
00:36:32,630 --> 00:36:35,430
It's nice. Buy it.

382
00:36:45,400 --> 00:36:48,070
I think... this model's probably pricey.

383
00:36:48,070 --> 00:36:49,600
The white one's limited edition.

384
00:36:52,030 --> 00:36:54,630
I just picked one up two weeks ago.

385
00:37:04,630 --> 00:37:07,870
Don't go anywhere, baby. Wait for Daddy.

386
00:37:21,830 --> 00:37:23,270
You're actually buying it?

387
00:37:24,870 --> 00:37:28,670
Yeah. And I'm shooting you with it right now. Be my model.

388
00:37:29,270 --> 00:37:30,600
No way.

389
00:37:30,600 --> 00:37:31,800
I hate photos of me.

390
00:37:32,930 --> 00:37:34,830
But I like taking pictures of you.

391
00:37:38,200 --> 00:37:40,270
Don't argue with the guy paying.

392
00:37:40,270 --> 00:37:42,770
Hold on, let me go pay first.

393
00:37:59,330 --> 00:38:01,530
Come on, everyone ready?

394
00:38:03,600 --> 00:38:05,970
You wanted content, didn't you?

395
00:38:05,970 --> 00:38:08,100
Don't worry about the venue.

396
00:38:08,100 --> 00:38:10,130
I know the owner.

397
00:38:19,570 --> 00:38:20,730
Ready?

398
00:38:22,500 --> 00:38:25,430
Three, two, one.

399
00:38:43,700 --> 00:38:49,700
♪ Have you ever felt it — no matter how far the days carry us ♪

400
00:38:49,700 --> 00:39:01,000
♪ Every time I think back on those nights, the memory warms my heart all over again ♪

401
00:39:01,000 --> 00:39:07,630
♪ Looking at the photos some nights before I sleep, I smile to myself ♪

402
00:39:07,630 --> 00:39:16,700
♪ Every time I think back on those nights, on you and me — a time I've never once forgotten ♪

403
00:39:18,830 --> 00:39:23,900
Save it for someone else. Shooting me is just a waste.

404
00:39:23,900 --> 00:39:28,730
Would you stop talking and hold still? I haven't taken a single shot.

405
00:39:28,730 --> 00:39:31,670
Oh, really? Okay, okay. / Pose.

406
00:39:36,400 --> 00:39:38,900
Yeah, that's good.

407
00:39:39,670 --> 00:39:41,330
Yeah, that's it. / Whoa.

408
00:39:41,330 --> 00:39:43,770
You sure you got it? / Yeah, yeah, it's great.

409
00:39:43,770 --> 00:39:45,400
I'm not so sure about this.

410
00:39:45,400 --> 00:39:46,470
A little more.

411
00:39:48,400 --> 00:39:50,930
Aren't you wasting film here?

412
00:39:56,370 --> 00:39:58,230
Come on, come here. There.

413
00:40:04,100 --> 00:40:05,270
Go all out.

414
00:40:07,300 --> 00:40:09,800
Okay, that's enough. Let me see. / Huh?

415
00:40:09,800 --> 00:40:11,800
Let me see the photo. / What?

416
00:40:11,800 --> 00:40:15,500
Let me see the photo. / See what? It's film. It has to be developed.

417
00:40:15,500 --> 00:40:17,030
Oh, really? / Yeah.

418
00:40:17,030 --> 00:40:20,800
Come on. I've got plenty more places I want to shoot you.

419
00:40:20,800 --> 00:40:22,070
I'll take you there.

420
00:40:22,070 --> 00:40:23,470
But first—

421
00:40:23,970 --> 00:40:26,330
You really don't want your picture taken, do you?

422
00:40:26,330 --> 00:40:29,070
No. I get shy.

423
00:40:40,000 --> 00:40:41,970
Is that what you want, Chemi?

424
00:40:45,770 --> 00:40:51,330
Yes. This color, this one's beautiful. But...

425
00:40:52,730 --> 00:40:55,900
looking at the price, I might have to ask them to hold it for me.

426
00:40:55,900 --> 00:40:57,670
It's a bit out of my league.

427
00:41:03,270 --> 00:41:06,700
Is there anything else you'd like, Chemi?

428
00:41:07,500 --> 00:41:10,570
Actually, I came today to look at guitar picks.

429
00:41:11,170 --> 00:41:12,700
Right, okay.

430
00:41:14,500 --> 00:41:18,170
They should be... right here.

431
00:41:20,530 --> 00:41:21,770
Here.

432
00:41:27,970 --> 00:41:29,600
Tony?

433
00:41:30,130 --> 00:41:32,100
Can I take a look at this one?

434
00:41:33,030 --> 00:41:35,870
That design just came in, kid.

435
00:41:35,870 --> 00:41:37,300
You've got a good eye.

436
00:41:41,300 --> 00:41:44,470
I've been hunting for this forever. Thought I'd missed it.

437
00:41:46,000 --> 00:41:47,630
It's beautiful.

438
00:41:48,070 --> 00:41:51,030
So what makes it special, Chemi?

439
00:41:52,500 --> 00:41:59,900
It is special. This is the exact brand and design the singer I love uses.

440
00:41:59,900 --> 00:42:02,170
I can't believe it's still here.

441
00:42:02,470 --> 00:42:06,330
Okay, then it's on me. Excuse me, I'd like to pay. / Sure, coming.

442
00:42:06,330 --> 00:42:08,970
No, wait, it's fine. I can buy this one myself.

443
00:42:08,970 --> 00:42:10,330
Ring it up, please.

444
00:42:10,330 --> 00:42:12,270
No, really, I'd feel bad.

445
00:42:12,270 --> 00:42:13,630
Ring it up, please.

446
00:42:13,630 --> 00:42:16,370
Look, this one's on me.

447
00:42:17,300 --> 00:42:21,330
As for that guitar, you'll have to save up for it yourself.

448
00:42:21,330 --> 00:42:23,170
Because I definitely can't afford that.

449
00:42:23,170 --> 00:42:24,730
So what's it going to be? Yes or no?

450
00:42:24,730 --> 00:42:26,900
Yes, please. Ring it up.

451
00:42:27,230 --> 00:42:28,770
You got it, kid.

452
00:42:51,200 --> 00:42:58,070
Are you sure about this? I'm really not confident. Let me shoot you instead.

453
00:43:01,100 --> 00:43:02,600
Stand right here.

454
00:43:02,600 --> 00:43:07,100
This is a film camera, right? How do I even use it?

455
00:43:07,730 --> 00:43:13,930
Here, it's not hard. See this? It's called the viewfinder.

456
00:43:13,930 --> 00:43:16,170
When you shoot, you look through here.

457
00:43:16,170 --> 00:43:18,530
And don't let your finger cover this — the flash.

458
00:43:18,530 --> 00:43:24,070
After you shoot, you wind it here. I've already wound it. You just press the shutter.

459
00:43:24,400 --> 00:43:25,500
Try lining it up.

460
00:43:26,700 --> 00:43:28,170
It's kind of blurry.

461
00:43:28,470 --> 00:43:29,670
Look properly.

462
00:43:30,830 --> 00:43:32,400
Oh, now it's clear.

463
00:43:33,800 --> 00:43:35,100
There you go.

464
00:43:37,000 --> 00:43:39,000
I'll stand right here.

465
00:43:39,000 --> 00:43:41,070
Okay.

466
00:43:44,830 --> 00:43:46,230
One second.

467
00:43:55,430 --> 00:43:59,800
Hey, I'm really not confident. What if I mess up the shot?

468
00:44:00,930 --> 00:44:05,930
It's fine, I did the math. It's the last frame exactly. Have a little confidence.

469
00:44:08,800 --> 00:44:11,000
I'm right here.

470
00:44:13,270 --> 00:44:14,670
Okay.

471
00:44:16,730 --> 00:44:19,200
One, two, three.

472
00:44:25,970 --> 00:44:28,730
Okay, that's it. How is it? Did it come out nice?

473
00:44:29,200 --> 00:44:30,570
How would I know?

474
00:44:31,470 --> 00:44:36,170
Let's go, I'm thirsty. Thank you kindly.

475
00:44:50,470 --> 00:44:54,470
That was so much fun. / It was fun. Something different.

476
00:44:54,830 --> 00:44:56,630
Oh, Fuen! Physics!

477
00:44:56,870 --> 00:44:58,100
Hey there, Star.

478
00:44:58,100 --> 00:44:59,800
Want to sit with me?

479
00:44:59,800 --> 00:45:00,800
Can we?

480
00:45:30,700 --> 00:45:33,130
So, are you here for tutoring?

481
00:45:33,130 --> 00:45:37,470
No, I came to eat with friends.

482
00:45:37,470 --> 00:45:39,270
But they've all gone home already.

483
00:45:41,230 --> 00:45:44,470
What about you two? What brings you here?

484
00:45:48,400 --> 00:45:50,700
We came to see a movie.

485
00:46:04,370 --> 00:46:05,570
Sorry.

486
00:46:05,570 --> 00:46:07,430
Star, you've got something on your lip.

487
00:46:22,000 --> 00:46:24,930
Oh, it's fine. I'll get it myself.

488
00:46:32,730 --> 00:46:36,100
Hey, I'm going to the bathroom. Be right back.

489
00:47:07,100 --> 00:47:10,830
"If you want to know what he's thinking, put your eyes to good use."

490
00:47:10,830 --> 00:47:14,670
"Look at him until he knows how you feel."

491
00:47:14,670 --> 00:47:16,900
"Good luck. I'm heading off."

492
00:47:18,630 --> 00:47:20,900
Sorry, Star, I have to head off.

493
00:47:20,900 --> 00:47:22,770
Oh — one second, Fuen.

494
00:47:22,770 --> 00:47:27,100
Tomorrow's Physics's birthday, isn't it?

495
00:47:28,200 --> 00:47:33,930
I want to buy him a present. Could you help me pick something?

496
00:47:38,300 --> 00:47:39,870
A present for Physics?

497
00:47:42,130 --> 00:47:44,730
Honestly, he's already got just about everything.

498
00:47:44,730 --> 00:47:48,470
So there's nothing he especially wants?

499
00:47:54,200 --> 00:47:56,670
Please... Fuen.

500
00:47:59,430 --> 00:48:02,570
Well, if it's something he wants...

501
00:48:08,230 --> 00:48:10,400
What is it?

502
00:48:22,330 --> 00:48:26,070
Thank you, Fuen, for helping me pick a present for Physics today.

503
00:48:38,970 --> 00:48:42,500
Was something wrong with Physics today?

504
00:48:42,500 --> 00:48:44,600
Why did he just walk off like that?

505
00:48:47,600 --> 00:48:49,600
Did you two have a fight?

506
00:48:51,400 --> 00:48:53,770
Not at all. Don't overthink it, Star.

507
00:48:54,570 --> 00:48:56,830
He just had something to deal with at home.

508
00:48:59,770 --> 00:49:02,400
If there's nothing else, I'll get going.

509
00:49:02,400 --> 00:49:06,230
Of course. Get home safe, Fuen.

510
00:49:15,170 --> 00:49:22,900
"2 Years ago"

511
00:49:44,430 --> 00:49:47,230
Ugh, you know I'm bad at driving.

512
00:49:47,230 --> 00:49:48,800
Why'd you drag me into this?

513
00:49:48,800 --> 00:49:51,330
Whoa. And that's you being bad at driving?

514
00:49:51,330 --> 00:49:53,730
You were just trying to overtake me back there.

515
00:49:56,100 --> 00:49:59,230
I'm done. I don't like driving.

516
00:50:01,100 --> 00:50:02,500
Okay.

517
00:50:02,500 --> 00:50:06,800
If you don't like driving, when we're older, I'll drive you around myself.

518
00:50:26,670 --> 00:50:28,300
Fuen.

519
00:50:29,930 --> 00:50:32,630
Did you forget something today?

520
00:50:38,970 --> 00:50:41,470
No. I turned in all my homework.

521
00:50:46,300 --> 00:50:48,070
Today's my birthday.

522
00:50:54,530 --> 00:50:57,630
What? Why didn't you say anything?

523
00:50:58,870 --> 00:51:01,430
I told you ages ago. You just forgot.

524
00:51:10,130 --> 00:51:13,030
There are 365 days in a year.

525
00:51:13,030 --> 00:51:15,870
Today I'm giving you whatever you want.

526
00:51:19,100 --> 00:51:20,570
Deal.

527
00:51:21,770 --> 00:51:23,430
Okay?

528
00:51:25,370 --> 00:51:27,970
Okay, then.

529
00:51:29,870 --> 00:51:32,570
Excuse me, returning the helmet.

530
00:51:35,730 --> 00:51:36,570
Thank you.

531
00:51:37,270 --> 00:51:38,830
What do you want to play next?

532
00:51:38,830 --> 00:51:40,870
Okay, first up—

533
00:51:42,270 --> 00:51:44,670
The basketball machine. / All right, go.

534
00:51:47,830 --> 00:51:51,870
Come on, come on! Put it up!

535
00:51:59,530 --> 00:52:01,270
Which one? / This one.

536
00:52:03,130 --> 00:52:05,330
Hey! / Is this thing rigged?

537
00:52:11,000 --> 00:52:13,700
Hey, grab the ball. / Oh.

538
00:52:34,830 --> 00:52:37,430
Here's your prize, sir.

539
00:52:40,000 --> 00:52:41,930
Whoa, thank you so much.

540
00:52:47,100 --> 00:52:49,030
The face is exactly the same.

541
00:52:49,030 --> 00:52:50,470
Same how?

542
00:52:50,470 --> 00:52:52,270
I said it's the same, so it's the same.

543
00:52:52,270 --> 00:52:54,100
Don't argue, kid.

544
00:52:54,100 --> 00:52:55,700
Whose birthday is it today?

545
00:53:00,170 --> 00:53:04,770
Consider it my birthday present to you.

546
00:53:06,000 --> 00:53:07,670
Thank you kindly.

547
00:53:11,500 --> 00:53:13,670
Yeah, it's identical.

548
00:53:14,470 --> 00:53:15,830
Identical how?

549
00:53:16,870 --> 00:53:18,600
Trust me. It's identical.

550
00:53:18,600 --> 00:53:21,230
Except this thing's face is a bit chubbier.

551
00:53:25,700 --> 00:53:28,770
Thanks for today, man.

552
00:54:00,270 --> 00:54:03,300
Bro, open the door.

553
00:54:05,470 --> 00:54:07,670
What is it? I'm going to bed.

554
00:54:08,700 --> 00:54:11,730
If you want to know, open the door.

555
00:54:13,730 --> 00:54:15,730
I don't want to. I'm sleeping.

556
00:54:22,600 --> 00:54:24,670
Hey, I'm sleeping!

557
00:54:33,130 --> 00:54:34,800
Chemi, what's going on?

558
00:54:37,300 --> 00:54:41,400
♪ Happy Birthday to you ♪

559
00:54:41,400 --> 00:54:45,130
♪ Happy Birthday to you ♪

560
00:54:45,130 --> 00:54:49,230
♪ Happy Birthday, Happy Birthday ♪

561
00:54:49,230 --> 00:54:53,330
♪ Happy Birthday to you ♪

562
00:54:53,330 --> 00:54:58,570
Make a wish before you blow them out. You always blow first — no wonder none of them come true.

563
00:55:23,070 --> 00:55:24,430
Hey. / Yeah?

564
00:55:24,430 --> 00:55:27,200
I forgot — I've got a series to finish.

565
00:55:27,200 --> 00:55:30,800
Right, and I'm at the part where the lead is winning him back.

566
00:55:30,800 --> 00:55:34,200
That's right, go on, go watch with me. / They're making up right now.

567
00:55:34,200 --> 00:55:35,830
Go on, go watch.

568
00:55:58,030 --> 00:56:00,030
Why did you sneak off early?

569
00:56:00,830 --> 00:56:03,770
You said you wanted to be with me today.

570
00:56:13,400 --> 00:56:14,830
Well...

571
00:56:16,000 --> 00:56:20,130
I thought you wanted to be with Star, so I got out of the way.

572
00:56:23,370 --> 00:56:25,370
So how did it go?

573
00:56:25,370 --> 00:56:27,700
That plan I told you about — did it work?

574
00:56:31,930 --> 00:56:34,270
Work? Are you kidding?

575
00:56:36,070 --> 00:56:41,670
I can't do it. You think that eye-contact thing is easy?

576
00:57:02,000 --> 00:57:04,200
It's not that hard.

577
00:57:06,300 --> 00:57:08,230
Here, let me show you.

578
00:57:09,330 --> 00:57:13,970
♪ When you turn to me, I can't hold your gaze for long ♪

579
00:57:13,970 --> 00:57:19,770
♪ I carry it into my dreams each night, but I can't do a thing about it ♪

580
00:57:19,770 --> 00:57:30,170
♪ The way you look at me shakes my heart even more — one slip and my mind wanders ♪

581
00:57:30,170 --> 00:57:41,270
♪ I slip and give you my heart, I slip and watch you every day — my heart can't take it ♪

582
00:57:42,200 --> 00:57:44,070
Not so hard, right?

583
00:57:50,300 --> 00:57:54,330
Hard. Even with you being my friend,

584
00:57:54,330 --> 00:57:56,100
I still couldn't do it.

585
00:58:00,270 --> 00:58:01,870
If it were Star,

586
00:58:02,800 --> 00:58:05,530
I'd suffocate and die.

587
00:58:13,430 --> 00:58:19,670
Then just stay standing right there. I'll come to you.

588
00:59:11,200 --> 00:59:17,000
"Eye contact — look until the other person notices."

589
00:59:37,530 --> 00:59:39,270
Keep it.

590
00:59:41,530 --> 00:59:44,270
Why do you always take these and make me keep them?

591
00:59:47,100 --> 00:59:47,930
Because...

592
00:59:49,570 --> 00:59:51,430
you asked me to help you win Star over.

593
00:59:56,430 --> 01:00:00,500
And you wanted to know how I'd go after someone.

594
01:00:05,800 --> 01:00:06,870
Fuen.

595
01:00:12,800 --> 01:00:14,900
When you like someone,

596
01:00:15,770 --> 01:00:19,500
you just put yourself close to them.

597
01:00:19,500 --> 01:00:23,930
However you can, as long as you don't make them uncomfortable.

598
01:00:23,930 --> 01:00:29,730
Because to me, you as you are right now is already the best there is.

599
01:00:36,730 --> 01:00:38,370
That's the third one now.

600
01:00:47,630 --> 01:00:48,430
Yeah.

601
01:00:49,070 --> 01:00:50,400
I know it's the third.

602
01:00:51,270 --> 01:00:54,100
The other two are in my room.

603
01:00:54,700 --> 01:00:55,870
They're not going anywhere.

604
01:01:02,370 --> 01:01:03,800
Fuen.

605
01:01:10,830 --> 01:01:13,000
You still haven't figured it out, have you?

606
01:01:28,000 --> 01:01:30,000
Oh! Chubby.

607
01:01:35,230 --> 01:01:38,300
I thought you'd thrown it out. I never see you use it.

608
01:01:41,770 --> 01:01:47,170
How could I throw it out? It's the first present you ever gave me.

609
01:02:03,430 --> 01:02:06,870
Okay. Want some cake? / Mm-hmm.

610
01:02:07,970 --> 01:02:09,930
Then I'll go down and get spoons.

611
01:02:11,700 --> 01:02:13,270
Hold it steady.

612
01:02:46,670 --> 01:02:51,770
♪ Something has begun, and it's getting complicated ♪

613
01:02:51,770 --> 01:03:05,900
♪ There's more to it than that, and I can't find the answer ♪

614
01:03:43,270 --> 01:03:48,230
"Look until the other person knows they're being watched."

615
01:03:48,430 --> 01:03:53,600
"You don't have to stay hung up on whoever it is you said isn't around to chase."

616
01:03:53,970 --> 01:03:56,970
I'm thinking we throw a mini concert in the heart of Siam.

617
01:03:56,970 --> 01:03:58,330
What brings you here today?

618
01:03:58,330 --> 01:03:59,430
We're here to sing.

619
01:03:59,430 --> 01:04:00,170
Go for it.

620
01:04:00,170 --> 01:04:01,330
Whoo!

621
01:04:02,370 --> 01:04:04,570
I know who can help us.

622
01:04:04,570 --> 01:04:05,430
Who?

623
01:04:05,430 --> 01:04:08,100
Going out with my little brother — pretty fun, right?

624
01:04:09,600 --> 01:04:13,600
I think I need to go train for our school's football team.

625
01:04:13,600 --> 01:04:15,930
You still won't accept Aof, will you?

626
01:04:15,930 --> 01:04:17,630
I don't want to see Chemi get hurt.

627
01:04:17,630 --> 01:04:19,730
Why the world-on-your-shoulders face?

628
01:04:19,730 --> 01:04:23,870
Heavier than the world. If I slip up even once, you can start planning my funeral.
